From 1c03b44a37b5f7724980a1bf23baf682a858382d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Casaroli <marco.casaroli@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:45:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mm/mm_heap: Do not run without the heap lock when a signal
 arrives.

mm_lock() returned 0 even when nxmutex_lock() failed.  nxmutex_lock()
returns -EINTR when a signal interrupts the wait, so a task that got a
signal while another task held the heap lock went on to change the heap
without the lock, and two tasks changed the free lists at the same
time.  With SMP this happened within seconds when processes were
created and reaped in parallel: SIGCHLD reached the parents while the
heap was busy, and the heap was corrupted.

Retry the lock when a signal interrupts it, and return the result.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Marco Casaroli <marco.casaroli@gmail.com>

diff --git a/mm/mm_heap/mm_lock.c b/mm/mm_heap/mm_lock.c
index a5a2c649..2776ee3e 100644
--- a/mm/mm_heap/mm_lock.c
+++ b/mm/mm_heap/mm_lock.c
@@ -104,13 +104,22 @@ int mm_lock(FAR struct mm_heap_s *heap)
     }
   else
     {
-      int ret = nxmutex_lock(&heap->mm_lock);
+      int ret;
+
+      /* A signal must not make the caller run without the lock */
+
+      do
+        {
+          ret = nxmutex_lock(&heap->mm_lock);
+        }
+      while (ret == -EINTR);
+
       if (ret >= 0)
         {
           kasan_bypass(true);
         }
 
-      return 0;
+      return ret;
     }
 }
 
